# `reporting/` — Human-owned communication artifacts

## Authority

The root [`README.md`](../README.md) contract defines placement, storage, and
lifecycle. Local [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) defines the human review gate.

```
reporting/
├── _assets/         # shared source style and generated theme adapters
├── papers/          # manuscript artifacts
├── posters/         # poster artifacts
├── presentations/   # talk/deck artifacts
└── writeups/        # internal reports and run interpretation
```

Each artifact has its own folder. Mutable source lives directly in that folder;
immutable external versions live in
`deliveries/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<milestone>/`. See
[`DELIVERIES.md`](DELIVERIES.md) for the universal freeze contract.

## Working-source rules

1. Reference canonical inputs while drafting. Data-derived figures come from
   `results/figures/{light,dark}/`; authored schematics come from
   `assets/figures/`. Do not claim every scientific figure is data-generated.
2. A number or claim must trace to real results and registered provenance; a
   citation must resolve to a real source. Agents may draft, but people own and
   approve scientific prose.
3. Shared TeX sources live in `_assets/`. Theme-color TeX is generated from
   `conf/theme/` and must not be edited by hand.
4. Working PDFs and build debris are disposable. Delivery payloads are frozen
   through the delivery command, checksum-manifested, and stored according to
   the Git/DVC size policy.

Per-type conventions: [`papers/`](papers/README.md),
[`posters/`](posters/README.md),
[`presentations/`](presentations/README.md), and
[`writeups/`](writeups/README.md).
